  "equipment_type": "Sensor (infrared gas analyzer)",
  "applies_to": "Teledyne 7500 and 7600 infrared gas analyzers with the Modbus communication function; channel registers CH1-CH8 apply to both models, CH9-CH12 to the 7600 only.",
  "summary": "The Teledyne 7500 and 7600 are multi-component infrared gas analyzers with a Modbus RTU port on RS-232 (RS-485 through an external converter). Each channel reports an integer concentration plus separate decimal-point and unit registers. This map covers all channel readings, range selection and the key/display command registers.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "The manual prints a register number (30001, 40001, 42001) and a relative address (0000H, 07D0H) and says the relative address sent in the message is the lower four digits of the register number minus 1."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Instruction Manual - Infrared Gas Analyzer Communication Functions (Modbus), Type 7500 / 7600",
    "doc_number": null,
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://teledyne-ai.com/en-us/Products_/Documents/Manuals/man_75007600comm.pdf",
    "pages": "specifications p. 4; relative address rule p. 7; function codes p. 11; data format pp. 23-24; address map pp. 25-30"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Concentrations are sent without a decimal point. Divide by 10^n where n is the channel's decimal-point register (0-3); the unit register gives vol%, ppm, mg/m3 or g/m3. Example in the manual: 1270 with decimal 2 and unit 0 = 12.70 vol%. Because the decimal place is per channel and range, the concentration registers are listed unscaled.",
    "Relevant model per the address map: R = 7500, K = 7600. Channel registers CH1-CH8 are marked for both models; CH9-CH12 and the CH5 range-change setting are 7600 only.",
    "Communication is fixed at 9600 bps, 8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit, RTU, over RS-232; up to 31 analyzers can share an RS-485 line through a converter.",
    "Readings are transmitted even when the display shows over-range dashes.",
    "Left out: the alarm/calibration status block from 30037 upward, whose rows are out of line in the source table, and the user-setting block 40001-40105 (calibration, alarm and timer settings)."
  ],
